{"step_index":556,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:54:13Z","input_tokens":3102,"cache_read_tokens":146490,"output_tokens":1591,"thinking":"Initial plan is to integrate private mode functionality and a theme toggle (light/dark) into the frontend application. The light mode logic involves retrieving the saved theme preference from local storage or defaulting to 'dark'. Setting the theme utilizes this saved preference, with an option to avoid triggering a transition effect.\n\nfunction toggleTheme() {\n    const currentTheme = document.body.classList.contains('theme-light') ? 'dark' : 'light';\n    setTheme(currentTheme, true);\n    localStorage.setItem('aegis_theme', currentTheme);\n}\n\nfunction setTheme(themeName, animate) {\n    document.body.classList.remove('theme-dark', 'theme-light');\n    document.body.classList.add(`theme-${themeName}`);\n\n    if (animate) {\n        document.body.classList.add('theme-transition');\n    } else {\n        document.body.classList.remove('theme-transition');\n    }\n\nNow design the Dark Mode logic. It will be the inverse of the Light Mode logic.\nLet's design the Private Mode logic.\n// Private Mode (Enable / Disable)\nfunction initPrivateMode() {\n    const isPrivate = localStorage.getItem('aegis_private') === 'true';\n    setPrivateMode(isPrivate);\n}\n\nfunction togglePrivateMode() {\n    const currentMode = localStorage.getItem('aegis_private') === 'true';\n    setPrivateMode(!currentMode);\n    localStorage.setItem('aegis_private', !currentMode);\n}\n\nfunction setPrivateMode(isPrivate) {\n    if (isPrivate) {\n        document.body.classList.add('private-mode');\n    } else {\n        document.body.classList.remove('private-mode');\n    }\n\nPrivate mode functionality hinges on checking an API endpoint for privacy status, which determines the application's visual state. The theme toggling logic ensures consistency across the application by updating both the `document.body` and `document.documentElement` classes. These updates reflect the theme choice in the DOM.\n\n\n\nInitial focus is on implementing the `updatePrivacyUI` function, which handles the visual representation of private mode. This involves updating text labels and button styles based on the private mode state, including header and tab button elements. Error handling is included to manage scenarios where fetching the private mode status fails.\n\n\nThe `updatePrivacyUI` function now dynamically updates UI elements based on private mode status, including banner visibility and text/button styling.  The `togglePrivateMode` function fetches privacy state from an API endpoint, updating the UI accordingly with appropriate auditory feedback and toast notifications. A `panicWipe` function has also been added which purges sensitive data via an API call and provides feedback.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"c:\\Users\\thann\\Downloads\\AntiGravity\\SpywareProcessMon\\frontend\\js\\app.js","Replacement":"// Initialize Application\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n    initClock();\n    initTheme();\n    initTabs();\n    initWebSocket();\n    checkPrivacyStatus();\n    runScan(true);","Target":"// Initialize Application\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n    initClock();\n    initTabs();\n    initWebSocket();\n    checkPrivacyStatus();\n    runScan(true);"}}]}
